Component Responsibility Composer / <code>tusk-framework/app</code> Creates an application project and installs its stable dependencies. Tusk Framework Owns application bootstrap, routes, dependency injection, validation, and request handling. Tusk Engine Validates project/runtime configuration, generates RoadRunner configuration at startup, starts and supervises RoadRunner, and reports readiness/health. RoadRunner Owns HTTP transport and PHP worker lifecycle. <p>Canonical flow:</p> <pre><code>composer create-project tusk-framework/app &lt;directory&gt;
cd &lt;directory&gt;
tusk doctor
tusk start
</code></pre> <p>The application entry point remains <code>bootstrap/app.php</code>. RoadRunner serves requests and manages PHP workers; the Engine is a runtime manager, not an HTTP proxy or a second worker pool. The skeleton's <code>/api/products</code> route is an example only and stores data in memory.</p>
